(5763462, 835862, 65319, '<td valign="top">Mark, <br/> <br/>Mmmmmm...yummy drama with a dark and mysterious hero...or is does he play the "heavy" anti-hero?  Ohhhh...the suspense!  I can''t wait for the movie.  My only nattering naybob nitpicking is on a couple of notes...this photo will suffer from those with uncalibrated monitors and your score will suffer along with it.  Also, with such a character...I''d like to see exactly that...MORE character.  I want to see some kind of deep raw emotion from The Old West (picture Clint Eastwood''s challenge "make my day" type of emotion).  I see you used the rain as a "prop" of sorts to add weather drama...love that idea!  However, to create more drama, I''d like to see the character interact more with the weather and how it''s affecting his MOOD!  Overall, your black and white photography carries strong weight and the obvious well-honed skills of a first class photographer.  <br/> <br/>The next time I see Clint...I''ll give him your number for a portrait!  ;-)</td>', 'Mark,  Mmmmmm...yummy drama with a dark and mysterious hero...or is does he play the "heavy" anti-hero?  Ohhhh...the suspense!  I can''t wait for the movie.  My only nattering naybob nitpicking is on a couple of notes...this photo will suffer from those with uncalibrated monitors and your score will suffer along with it.  Also, with such a character...I''d like to see exactly that...MORE character.  I want to see some kind of deep raw emotion from The Old West (picture Clint Eastwood''s challenge "make my day" type of emotion).  I see you used the rain as a "prop" of sorts to add weather drama...love that idea!  However, to create more drama, I''d like to see the character interact more with the weather and how it''s affecting his MOOD!  Overall, your black and white photography carries strong weight and the obvious well-honed skills of a first class photographer.   The next time I see Clint...I''ll give him your number for a portrait!  ;-)', '2009-12-10 21:40:38.000000', NULL, 0),
